;
; Minimal .def file for the subset of Windows PathCch* APIs QEMU's
; util/cutils.c actually calls (PathCchSkipRoot), used to synthesize a
; libpathcch.a import library with `zig dlltool` when cross-compiling
; for Windows with `zig cc` (see scripts/build-with-zig-cc-windows.sh).
;
; zig's bundled mingw-w64 subset ships the underlying Windows 10+ API-set
; forwarder DLL's own .def file
; (lib/libc/mingw/lib-common/api-ms-win-core-path-l1-1-0.def) but not the
; "libpathcch.a" friendly-name alias that a full mingw-w64 distribution
; normally provides and that QEMU's meson.build looks up via
; `cc.find_library('pathcch', required: true)`. This file re-exports the
; same symbol list (verbatim from that .def) under the "pathcch" name so
; `-lpathcch` resolves; the real functions are still served at runtime by
; api-ms-win-core-path-l1-1-0.dll (present on Windows 10+ and forwarded to
; kernelbase.dll), exactly as a real libpathcch.a would.
;
LIBRARY api-ms-win-core-path-l1-1-0

EXPORTS

PathAllocCanonicalize
PathAllocCombine
PathCchAddBackslash
PathCchAddBackslashEx
PathCchAddExtension
PathCchAppend
PathCchAppendEx
PathCchCanonicalize
PathCchCanonicalizeEx
PathCchCombine
PathCchCombineEx
PathCchFindExtension
PathCchIsRoot
PathCchRemoveBackslash
PathCchRemoveBackslashEx
PathCchRemoveExtension
PathCchRemoveFileSpec
PathCchRenameExtension
PathCchSkipRoot
PathCchStripPrefix
PathCchStripToRoot
PathIsUNCEx
